\[
V=\dfrac{1}{3}\pi(4.8)^2(3.6+6.4)=\dfrac{1}{3}\pi\cdot23.04\cdot10=76.8\pi\approx\boxed{241.3}\text{ cubic units}.
\]

A longer chord is closer to the centre, so the chord of length $16$ is nearest the centre. Let it be at distance $d$ from the centre $O$; then the chord of length $k$ is at distance $d+2$ and the chord of length $12$ at distance $d+4$. With radius $r$, the half-chords give
\[
r^2=8^2+d^2=6^2+(d+4)^2 .
\]
So $64+d^2=36+d^2+8d+16$, hence $8d=12$, $d=\dfrac{3}{2}$ and $r^2=64+\dfrac{9}{4}=\dfrac{265}{4}$.

